{
    "m_SGVersion": 0,
    "m_Type": "UnityEditor.ShaderGraph.StickyNoteData",
    "m_ObjectId": "95c406c38f764e64bb2b24002c5cf9bc",
    "m_Title": "Lambda calculation for Smith's microfacet shadowing and masking functions",
    "m_Content": "Side note: There is never a lower value then 0, since 0 asdalready gives us the darkest shade possible\n\n1. Cos θ = normal * Lightvector\nMax 1e-5, Cos θ\n\n2. Tan θ = Sin θ / Cos θ\nor Tan θ = sqr(1 - Cos² θ) / Cos θ\nbecause:\nSin² θ + Cos² θ = 1 -> Sin θ = sqr(1 - Cos² θ)\nMax 1e-5, Tan θ\n\n3. Get Tangent through the Normal\nDotproduct of Normal and Tangent has to be 0\nIf Normal.Z != 0\nthen (1, 1, -(Normal.X + Normal.Y) / Normal.Z)\nelse (1, -X / Y, 1)\n\n4. Get Bitangent\nNormalize Normal and Tangent\nNormal x Tangent = Bitangent\n\n5. Calculate Cos ϕ & Sin ϕ\nω = Incoming Lightvector\nωt = dot(ω, tangent)\nωb = dot(ω, bitangent)\n\nCos ϕ = ωt / sqr(ωt² + ωb²)\nSin ϕ =  ωb / sqr(ωt² + ωb²)\nBUT\nOur formular is using Cos² ϕ and Sin² ϕ. Thats why we can calculate this:\nCos² ϕ = ωt² / ωt² + ωb²\nSin² ϕ =  ωb² / ωt² + ωb²\n\n6. Get projected anisotropic roughness (α)\n- set Variables\nfloat roughness // range(0, 1) fix value\nfloat anisotropy // range(-1, 1) fix value\n- calculate\nfloat aspect = sqrt(1.0 - 0.9 * anisotropy);  // controls elliptical stretch\r\nfloat alphaX = roughness / aspect;\r\nfloat alphaY = roughness * aspect;\n\n7. Get the anisotropic roughness\nalphaX == αx\nalphaY == αy\n\nα = sqr(α²x * Cos²ϕ + α²y * Sin²ϕ )\n\n8. Calculate a\na = 1 / max(1e-5, α * tan θ)\n\n9. Lambda function to create return value\nif a < 1.6\nthen return (1 - 1,259 * a + 0,396 * a²) / (3.535 * a * 2,181 * a²)\nelse return 0",
